IMPLEMENTATION: Schema for the initial `AppDbContext` (single `20260817112734_InitialCreate` migration) matches `Course`/`TaskEntity` and looks correct for a Sprint 1 deadline tracker: both tables have GUID primary keys, `TaskEntities.CourseId` is a nullable FK to `Courses` (fine, since not every task is course-linked yet) and `ParentTaskId` is a self-referencing FK supporting the subtask hierarchy already modelled on `TaskEntity.ChildrenTasks`. One thing to keep an eye on: no unique constraint on `Courses.Code`, so nothing stops a duplicate course code being seeded or created later - not a blocker at this stage since seeding is still hardcoded, but worth an index/unique constraint once real user input creates courses.

REVIEW: Confirmed - the FK/PK layout is evidence-backed by the PRAGMA dump and correctly reflects the two-table Sprint 1 shape. The `Courses.Code` uniqueness gap is a legitimate, low-severity follow-up rather than a blocking issue; agree it shouldn't hold up this PR. No further changes recommended.

